.TH RUA\-TOOL 1 "2026-11-24" "rua-tool" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rua\-tool \- find DMARC reports pointed at expired domains and disclose them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rua\-tool
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rua\-tool
inspects the DMARC record published at
.IR _dmarc. <domain>
and checks the domains that its aggregate
.RB ( rua )
and forensic
.RB ( ruf )
reports are sent to. If a report address points at a
.B registrable domain that is unregistered
(or about to expire), an attacker could register it and begin receiving that
organisation's DMARC reports \(em leaking mail infrastructure and aiding
spoofing. The tool can scan a single domain, spider a site to harvest and scan
many domains, and draft responsible\-disclosure notices for the affected
webmasters.
.PP
Report addresses are reduced to their registrable domain (eTLD+1) via the
Public Suffix List before checking, so
.I x@sub.example.co.uk
is checked as
.IR example.co.uk .
Registration is checked with RDAP (falling back to DNS when RDAP is
inconclusive). All lookups are read\-only and the tool never sends mail.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "check " domain
Look up a domain's DMARC record and check its rua/ruf report domains.
.TP
.BI "spider " url
Crawl a site within its own registrable domain, harvest every referenced
domain, and scan each one.
.TP
.BI "scan\-list " file
Scan a newline\-delimited list of domains (blank lines and # comments ignored).
.TP
.B list
Show stored findings.
.TP
.BI "contact " domain
Discover a responsible\-disclosure contact (security.txt, then RDAP, then role
accounts).
.TP
.B report
Write disclosure e\-mail drafts for stored findings.
.TP
.B version
Print the build version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output (check, spider, list).
.TP
.BR \-\-save ", " \-\-no\-save
Persist (or skip persisting) findings to the store. spider and scan\-list save
by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-pages= N
Spider: maximum pages to crawl (default 25; 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-depth= N
Spider: maximum link depth (default 2; 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BI \-\-delay= SEC
Spider: politeness delay between requests in seconds (default 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-domain= X
report: only build drafts for this scanned domain.
.TP
.BI \-\-out= DIR
report: output directory (default ./reports).
.TP
.BI \-\-from= NAME
report: sign\-off name in the drafts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, no findings.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
One or more findings present.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUA_STORE
Path to the findings JSON store (default ./rua-findings.json).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable coloured output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check one domain:
.B rua\-tool check example.com
.TP
Spider a site with no page limit:
.B rua\-tool spider https://example.com \-\-max\-pages=0
.TP
Draft disclosure notices for everything found:
.B rua\-tool report \-\-from="Your Name"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./rua-findings.json
Default findings store (override with
.BR RUA_STORE ).
.SH SEE ALSO
RFC 7489 (DMARC). Project home: https://github.com/joegarbett/rua-tool
.SH AUTHOR
Joseph Garbett
